 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "roomba e5 wont charge properly, sometimes it does sometimes it doesnt"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Intermittent charging in Roombas is most often caused by poor connection rather than a broken battery. The most common culprit is dust or oxidation on the gold charging contacts located on the bottom of the robot and inside the charging base. Please unplug the base from the wall for safety, then check if these metal points are dirty. If they look clean but it still fails to charge reliably, we will next check whether the power adapter itself is providing consistent voltage."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok, the contacts on the dock are dull with a greasy grey film and there's loads of hair round the ones on the robot. no heat or smell from it. app says Charging error 5"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That greasy film and hair buildup is probably why you're getting Charging Error 5; it prevents a reliable electrical connection between the robot and the base. Since there's no heat or smell, the internal electronics are likely fine, but the dirty contacts need to be cleaned properly. Please unplug the charging base for safety, then use a cotton bud or cloth with a little white vinegar (or rubbing alcohol) to scrub the gold plates on both the robot and the dock until they shine, removing all hair and residue. Dry them completely, plug it back in, place the robot on the dock, and tell me if you see a solid green light indicating it is charging."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok did that, wiped them with isopropyl and dried. been charging every night for 4 days now, no error"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That is excellent news. The greasy film and hair were most likely blocking the connection, causing Error 5. To keep it charging reliably, just give those gold contacts a quick wipe with a dry cloth once or twice a month to stop dust building up again. Is there anything else I can help you with regarding your Roomba?"
  }
 ],
